,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":-0.0237,"r5":0.0363,"r1_spy":-0.0267,"r5_spy":0.0355}}],"quotes":[{"c":"LPX 2018 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2018-11-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"During the quarter, we achieved strong price realization relative to random links, despite volume and pricing headwinds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/06/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2018-11-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"We continue to experience softer demand for I-Joist and for LVL as well as higher cost of sales, which have outpaced average price increases for these products.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/06/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2018-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael Kinney","x":"In 2019, they -- we will actually incur probably more cost in terms of severance and the move cost and the (inaudible) transition people from one location to another location, you're going to end up having an overlap of that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/06/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2018-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"So I see this as -- while we definitely have some cost savings baked in to our expectations, while consolidating all those activities here, we will find efficiency and productivity improvements, but just by having it all consolidated in one place.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/06/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2019-02-13","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"And as Brad noted, the decline in EWP sales was driven by weaker housing starts, resulting in lower volumes across all product lines although we maintained most of our price increases from earlier in the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/13/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2019-02-13","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"We have seen demand respond back in the South, as the weather has been a little bit better than in the North and that's where we've seen the price increases that reported in Random.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/13/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2019-02-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"Our cost reduction initiatives are focused on three areas: increasing the efficiency of our mills by improving productivity, run time and quality through our OEE initiative; applying best practices to our supply chain including procurement, logistics and working capital across $1.1 billion of…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/13/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2018 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2019-02-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Other operating charges include $5 million of severance related to reorganizations within our corporate offices and $5 million related to property damage sustained by our Wilmington, South Carolina facility during the Hurricane Florence.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/13/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2018-earnings-confer.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2019-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan J.M. Haughie","x":"The volume reduction had minimal impact on EBITDA, given the EWP's low margins whereas the price increase flow directly through, thereby resulting in an EBITDA increase of $2 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q1-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2019-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Bradley Southern","x":"George, we went out this year with a similar pricing -- price increase strategy as we implemented last year, same timing March 1, and we are looking into this year as having similar results around the price improvement that we saw last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q1-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2019-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan J.M. Haughie","x":"…the negative impacts from lower volumes in EWP and the Dawson conversion were offset by a combination of cost reduction actions and the improvement in product mix, inherent in replacing low margin EWP with higher margin SmartSide Strand plus neutralizing everything with the OSB price reduction.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q1-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Bradley Southern","x":"Single-family housing starts fell by 3% in the first quarter, where we posted a healthy 13% growth held by our customers pre-buy ahead of our March price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Now this includes the benefit of the March price increase and normal seasonal demand patterns, but the fact remains the quarter-over-quarter, both volume and price increased for SmartSide Strand while the opposite is true for OSB.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"These were partly offset by $2 million of severance charges, including $1 million due to the indefinite curtailment of production at our Peace Valley mill in British Columbia.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"After removing the warranty income and the severance charges and then normalizing the tax rate our non-GAAP earnings per share is $0.11.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"John, so the main driver for that lowering guidance long-term per Siding is our expectation that the housing recovery has slowed and will continue to be rather flat to slight increases versus a little more aggressive housing recovery that we had forecasted over the past couple of years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2019-08-06","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"But I'd also like to try, but I feel as though we've kind of lowered the guidance $150 to $180 was the range of tightened out to $161, $170, I think will come in at the low end of that tightened range.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2019-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"And admittedly, this includes some benefit from the March price increase and seasonal demand patterns.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2019-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Other charges and credits of $9 million comprised of $5 million impairment charge and $4 million of severance charges, $2 million of which relate to the curtailment of our OSB mill in Peace Valley British Columbia and $2 million for reorganizations within our corporate offices.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2019-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Removing the impairment and severance charges and normalizing the tax rate, results in non-GAAP net income of $10 million for the quarter and non-GAAP earnings per share of $0.08.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q3-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2020-02-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Bradley Southern","x":"Also, we made a change this year, and we've talked about this on the call previously, but we made a change on the timing of our price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2020-02-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Bradley Southern","x":"The last few years, we've been raising prices to most customers on March 1.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2019 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2020-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"ALAN HAUGHIE","x":"Phase one of LP's capital allocation plan was to rightsize the cash balance by returning a significant amount of capital to shareholders.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/11/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2019-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2020-05-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"Regrettably, this has resulted in layoffs for some of our mill employees.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q1-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2020-05-05","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"I think that it's just I know if we're looking at projected growth rates and the fact that we've withdrawn our guidance for Siding, it's just kind of muddled right now to figure out what's going on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q1-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2020-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"OSB EBITDA of $46 million was $49 million higher than prior year, including $37 million of price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2020-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"And so I see a good outlook from a demand scenario for that business in the near-term but there's going to be margin squeezes as a result of the raw material price increases that we've been seeing and enjoying on the OSB side.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"As a result, we have written off $10 million of fiber inventory and paid $4 million of fiber assets, and incurred $2 million in severance costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2020-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"And we put a hiring freeze in place, which is still in place and will be in place for a while, probably at least in the next budget season.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q2-2020-earnings-call-t.aspx"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2021-02-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"However, given the operating leverage and pricing power inherent in the business, we are raising our long-term target for the Siding EBITDA margin by 5 percentage points to 25%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2020-earnings-call-t/"},{"c":"LPX 2020 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2021-02-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"We announced a price increase, Ketan, that was effective January 1.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/16/louisiana-pacific-corp-lpx-q4-2020-earnings-call-t/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2021-05-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"So I would say it's but we've probably gotten a little bit stronger price realization on the back end of the increase than we've gotten in prior years, but it's just a the strength of the demand right now is able to hold on -- allowed us to hold on some of that list pricing that we increased at…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/lp-building-solutions-lpx-q1-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2021-05-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"So I would -- from a modeling standpoint, I would say, if you carry over where we are right now and give us a little bit of leeway on mix, it would be a pretty good way of looking at the rest of the year as far as our price increase realization.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/lp-building-solutions-lpx-q1-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"LP South America segment also had a very strong quarter with OSB and Siding price increases more than offsetting raw material cost inflation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/louisiana-pacific-corporation-lpx-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2021-08-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Notably the 9% price increase in the quarter includes four percentage points from annual list price increases and three points on the packet that is from reduced discounts and rebates.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/03/louisiana-pacific-corporation-lpx-q2-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2021-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brad Southern","x":"While we have benefited from higher OSB prices, some of those gains are now being offset by higher prices and tight availability for resins and freight where we have seen meaningful price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/louisiana-pacific-corporation-lpx-q3-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"LPX 2021 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2021-11-02","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"For the third quarter, these new higher value-added products made up 10% of Siding volume, 15% of Siding revenue and contributed three points of the 9% price increases for the segment. slide 10 shows the quarter in more detail for our OSB business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/louisiana-pacific-corporation-lpx-q3-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2025-11-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"The $2 million tariff impact is the retiree tariffs Louisiana-Pacific Corporation had been paying to import expert finish into Canada.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/06/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2025-11-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Those tariffs were rescinded in late August, so we are not currently incurring that expense.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/06/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2025-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"Price realization fared somewhat better than expected due to a combination of the lag in contact oil prices and structural solutions mix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/06/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2025-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan Haughie","x":"So all else equal, price realization in the fourth quarter will likely provide less of a tailwind than it did in the third.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/06/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2026-02-17","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alan J. Haughie","x":"The only other items to note for Siding in the fourth quarter chart are the absence of tariffs on the Expert Finish we are importing into Canada, and the non-recurrence of last year's effects from production and cost timing due to the delayed maintenance project last fall.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/17/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2026-02-17","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Alan J. Haughie","x":"SG&A increases, tariffs, and other factors totaled about $23,000,000.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/17/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2026-02-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan J. Haughie","x":"As Jason said in his remarks, an acute lack of data, particularly housing starts, added uncertainties to our planning for volume allocations following the announcement of our 2026 price increase last October.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/17/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2025 Q4","e":"lpx","d":"2026-02-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Alan J. Haughie","x":"However, we expect average selling prices in the first quarter to be up six to eight points as a result of list price increases and the positive mix effect of ongoing Expert Finish growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/17/louisiana-pacific-lpx-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2026-05-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jason Ringblom","x":"In the current environment, we are taking a wait-and-see approach, no different than our approach to tariffs last year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/lpx-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jason Ringblom","x":"Price realization both in Siding and OSB exceeded our expectations, partially offsetting lower volumes and contributing to EBITDA performance above the high end of our guided range.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/lpx-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q1","e":"lpx","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jason Ringblom","x":"By contrast, the pricing power of SmartSide helped offset lower sales volume, moderating revenue declines.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/lpx-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2026-08-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Aaron Howald","x":"Just like we wouldn't make a long-term Siding decision based on short-term OSB volatility, we would be reluctant to make a long-term Siding investment based on tweet about tariff policy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/louisiana-pacific-lpx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2026-08-05","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Mark Weintraub","x":"And just since Maniwaki, I think was characterized as lead dog by Jason, is it fair to conclude that like these new Canadian tariffs that were announced, they don't have any impact on Siding?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/louisiana-pacific-lpx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2026-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jason Ringblom","x":"This brings me to the $14 million EBITDA drag from inflationary costs and other items, a little over half of which is from crude oil price increases flowing through our raw material supply chain, broadly in line with the sensitivities we discussed on the prior quarter's call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/louisiana-pacific-lpx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q2","e":"lpx","d":"2026-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jason Ringblom","x":"Unlike Siding, freight is a pass-through for OSB and the comparatively lower raw material demands compared to Siding led to smaller inflationary impacts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/05/louisiana-pacific-lpx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2026-11-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Aaron Howald","x":"With the large rebate and mix benefits from earlier in the year normalizing as expected, higher prices in Q3 were driven primarily by list price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/03/louisiana-pacific-lpx-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"LPX 2026 Q3","e":"lpx","d":"2026-11-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Aaron Howald","x":"Given the timing of price increases late in the quarter and LP's typical lag as prices move, we expec